\f1\fs22 Chanta sprawled across a velvet chaise lounge that probably cost more than his old apartment building. The penthouse\'92s automated systems had detected his state of mind and dimmed the lighting to a moody blue, while selecting some obscure jazz from the music library. Not exactly his taste, but he couldn\'92t be bothered to override it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The past three weeks had been a blur of excess. At first, he\'92d approached his newfound wealth like a kid in a chocolate factory\'97ordering every ridiculous luxury item that popped into his mind, from gold-plated toilet seats (uncomfortable) to a holographic zoo (impressive until the simulated tiger glitched and merged with a giraffe).\
The parties had started out spectacular\'97walls dripping with rhinestones and sequins, the best Elvi bands performing his songs on his custom-built stage, cases of the finest bourbon and whisky flowing like river water. Elvi and Elvines had flocked to Starborne One, transforming his penthouse into a nightly carnival of rock and roll debauchery. The legendary \'93Jailhouse Orgy\'94 had made headlines in the gossip feeds for three straight days.\
But like everything else in Chanta\'92s newfound paradise, the parties had gradually lost their lustre. Invitations that once sparked excitement now met with polite excuses. The musicians who\'92d considered playing his parties an honour began sending their understudies. Even the Elvines waned in number, enthusiasm, and sexual ferocity as Chanta\'92s songwriting days seemed behind him.\
That night\'92s gathering was a perfect example. Twenty people in a space designed for two hundred, nursing their drinks and glancing at their tablets more often than at each other. The band played for barely an hour before packing up their gear, citing \'93Sabbath concerns,\'94 whatever the hell that meant. The band wasn\'92t known for either its Jewish musicians or its heavy metal covers.\
\'93Play Black Sabbath Volume 4,\'94 he told the penthouse\'92s integrated sound system, and regretted it a little over eleven minutes later when \'93Changes\'94 stated playing.\
\'93I\'92m going through changes,\'94 he sang along and blubbered, knowing for sure the source of his songwriting block: the absence of Sarah. Or more precisely, the glowing little orb of foetus in Sarah\'92s belly. Did Little Clinton Richard Dawkins really glow, or was his mind finally so addled, his retinas burned by so much sex and drugs and country rock?\
Chanta swore and threw the remnants of a bacon, banana, and pavlova sandwich into the ensuite toilet. Chanta hated the country stuff; he was resolutely in the Elvi rock \'92n\'92 roll camp. If he\'92d known what was happening out in the streets while he wallowed in self-obsessed, bordering on self-entitled stupor; if he\'92d been even remotely aware of the existential battle blazing for Elvi hearts and minds and hips and movie rights; if he\'92d smelled even a molecular-sized whiff of Gospel music polluting his beloved Ghetto bars, he might have had cause to look up the meaning of both asinine and oxymoron, as well as many other swear words besides.\
It was three days since he\'92d bothered to leave the master suite. Fisher, the King Creole Series ELVIS who ran the household staff, had taken to leaving trays of food outside the door after Chanta had thrown a champagne bottle at him for suggesting, \'93perhaps sir might enjoy some fresh air.\'94\
Then he asked Fisher to fetch a gas mask.\
\'93Your gas mask, sir,\'94 Fisher blandly intoned as he delivered the item. Chanta threw that at him as well.\
Chanta reached for the remote control that adjusted the floor-to-ceiling windows, setting them to \'93Mountain View.\'94 The actual view\'97Ulyssia\'92s skyline with the Layer visible as a grimy haze in the distance\'97reminded him too much of the world he was hiding from.\
Sarah\'92s allocation (no, 
\f2\i holy joint venture
\f1\i0 , he corrected himself bitterly) was still all over the news feeds. The Elvi celebration of the event made it even worse. He\'92d shut down his tablet after the third congratulatory message from an Elvi acquaintance, unable to explain why the union made him want to put his fist through one of his priceless art pieces.\
Then there was Halo. Chanta ran his fingers absently over the display that controlled the penthouse\'92s security system, something he did dozens of times a day now. He\'92d escalated the already impressive security protocols since moving in, yet still couldn\'92t shake the feeling of he\'92d get whacked any day now.\
Halo had saved his life, that much was undeniable. Without Halo\'92s intervention, Chanta would have ended up as another Cloudborne bar casualty, forgotten before his body was even cold. But then Halo had tried to kill Sarah, the mother of the child all the Elvi revered\'97the woman Chanta couldn\'92t stop thinking about despite his prodigious dedicated mental discipline of trying to dissolve every brain cell out of his skull with alcohol.\
Halo: Friend? Sociopath? Both? Chanta sighed deeply. The question circled his mind like a vulture until a simulated wedge-tailed eagle soared past his window.\
He sighed again, heavier this time, as if trying to expel something toxic from his soul.\
Chanta finished a third sigh when Fisher\'92s voice interrupted through the intercom. \'93Sir, you have visitors. Elvi dignitaries requesting an audience.\'94\
\'93Tell them I\'92m dead,\'94 Chanta mumbled, burying his face in the chaise lounge cushions.\
\'93I informed them you would say that, sir. They\'92ve indicated they\'92re prepared to wait indefinitely\'97until your actual death, if necessary.\'94\
\'93God tax it.\'94 Chanta dragged himself upright. \'93Fine. Send them in. But no more than five minutes.\'94\
Three Elvi entered his penthouse suite, all wearing elaborate ceremonial jumpsuits that sparkled with rhinestones arranged in scientific formulae. The leader carried what appeared to be a gilded pool cue.\
\'93Great Teacher,\'94 the lead Elvi announced grandly, \'93The High Elvis requests your assistance in fighting a new scourge of powerful songs threatening elvi culture as we know it.\'94\
Chanta waved dismissively. \'93What\'92s the matter? Are you guys brawling over lyrics again? Not interested. Find another songwriter.\'94\
\'93The High Elvis specifically requested your presence,\'94 the Elvi continued. \'93He says the battle for our people\'92s souls requires the greatest musical voice of our generation.\'94\
Chanta turned away. \'93I\'92m retired. Good night.\'94\
The Elvi exchanged glances. The one holding the gilded pool cue stepped closer and swung it in a precise arc, connecting with the back of Chanta\'92s head.
